{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark thou traveler bold who dost set sail\nFor Japan where wonders manifold prevail\nLet mine words be thy guide through lands most fair\nAs through this quill-planned journey thou dost stare.\n\n**Upon the First Day thou dost arrive**\nAt Narita’s gates where skies in twilight glide\nTo Tokyo’s heart thou shalt repair apace\nWhere neon lights do dance in night’s embrace.\n\nAt Shibuya’s cross where crowds in throng do meet\nA thousand dreams in flickering lights repeat\nThen to Shinjuku’s bustle bold and bright\nWhere towering signs do pierce the starry night.\n\n**On the Morn of Second Day thou shalt arise**\nAnd seek the sacred grounds of Meiji’s shrine\nWhere spirits whisper through the ancient trees\nAnd torii gates stand ‘gainst the morning breeze.\n\nTo Harajuku’s streets where trending fashions play\nAnd Takeshita’s lane doth swell with giddy sway\nYet heed well dear guest let not thy purse grow thin\nFor treasures here are dear as gold within.\n\n**The Third Day calls thee forth to Asakusa’s grace**\nWhere temples old in mist do softly trace\nSenso-ji’s halls where lanterns gleam so bright\nAnd merchants call with voices sharp and light.\n\nBy Sumida’s river let thine eyes take flight\nFor Edo’s charm still lingers through the night\nA cruise upon the water calms thy soul\nAs Tokyo’s skyline stands in silent goal.\n\n**On the Fourth Day thou shalt embark anew**\nFor Kyoto’s gates where history doth brew\nAt Kiyomizu’s temple high above\nThe city sprawls like jewels on silver love.\n\nTo Fushimi’s shrine where sake’s sweet song doth flow\nAnd bamboo forests sway in winds that blow\nAt Arashiyama’s edge where time doth cease\nAnd monkeys chatter ‘neath the ancient trees.\n\n**The Fifth Day dawns with gold upon thy sight**\nAt Kinkaku-ji’s halls of gilded light\nWhere ponds reflect the heavens so serene\nAnd every step feels dear to hearts unseen.\n\nThrough Higashiyama’s streets where tea houses hide\nAnd geisha ghosts may still in shadows glide\nAt Gion’s heart where lanterns softly burn\nThe past and present in their grace do turn.\n\n**Now lo thy Sixth Day calls thee to Nara’s plain**\nWhere deer do roam with gentle step and gain\nAt Todai-ji’s hall where Buddha’s might\nDoth tower o’er the earth with boundless light.\n\nThe Great Stupa’s shade where ancient tales are told\nOf emperors and gods both fierce and bold\nYet pause and heed the deer that come so near\nWith eyes like embers begging bread so dear.\n\n**Upon the Seventh Day let thy heart take wing**\nTo Osaka’s port where dreams in steel do cling\nDotonbori’s glow where neon rivers run\nAnd takoyaki balls do sizzle one by one.\n\nAt Osaka Castle’s walls where warriors tread\nAnd legends rise from chronicles long dead\nYet taste the delights this city doth bestow\nWhere flavors dance and fires brightly glow.\n\n**Now farewell dear traveler as thy days grow few**\nFor Hiroshima’s peace awaits thee anew\nAt Itsukushima’s shrine where torii doth rise\nAmidst the mist and tides that claim the skies.\n\nThe Atomic Dome stands as solemn art\nA warning carved where hope and sorrow part\nYet Miyajima’s lights upon the bay\nDo paint the waves in colors bright as day.\n\n**Thy final morn shall find thee in Kyoto’s care**\nAt Kyoto Station where thy journey’s snare\nDoth tighten once more as trains prepare to call\nYet linger here and drink the last of all.\n\nFor Kyoto’s grace like cherry blossoms fades\nYet in thy heart its beauty never aids\nNow take thy leave with memories so sweet\nAnd let thy tale of Japan’s grandeur repeat.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " thou", "logprob": -2.7992587089538574}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.6179838180541992}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.004587126895785332}, {"token": " bold", "logprob": -0.47304725646972